**About IIHS Campus Development** 




 The IIHS Campus is located on a 54\-acre site at Kengeri, Bengaluru, located between a 525




 acre reserve forest and an 800\-year old 150\-acre lake. Its digitally augmented buildings and




 facilities will enable interdisciplinary teaching\-learning, research and practice, and




 demonstrate the best examples of Indian design and crafts. The Campus will provide faculty,




 students, and researchers with the opportunity to immerse themselves in and innovate




 around India’s core urban challenges.










 The Campus features a robust integrated digital infrastructure and services network




 supported by various sensors, and IoT devices to enable cost\-effective monitoring of high




 performance and sustainability. This will be enabled via an intelligent digital twin to integrate




 all building and campus\-wide services to assist in predictive operations and maintenance.










 The IIHS Campus Development team focuses on the planning, design, procurement,




 execution, and documentation of the development of the IIHS Kengeri Campus. Joining the




 Campus Development team at IIHS offers a unique opportunity to be at the forefront of




 building one of India’s most ambitious, sustainable and climate\-resilient campuses. Situated




 in the upcoming Kengeri area of Bengaluru, it is deeply rooted in principles of net neutrality




 and long\-term environmental stewardship, targeting Factor Two to Four infrastructure and




 services and ecological conservation. It also includes a range of iconic buildings and facilities,




 including the largest urban reference Library in Asia, a Metropolitan Museum and Ecological




 Interpretation Centre, a multi\-material and advanced Technology Maker Centre, a specialised




 kitchen that uses a green supply chain, and a future Convention Centre and Incubation




 Centre.










 As part of this fast\-paced and dynamic team, you will gain hands\-on experience and




 unparalleled exposure to interdisciplinary planning, design, and implementation spanning




 various technology domains, architecture, urban design, planning, ecological, and




 environmental design, ICT and IoT. The role is designed to accelerate your professional




 development, offering meaningful engagement with cutting\-edge practices in sustainable and




 climate\-resilient development, and biodiversity conservation. We are looking for candidates




 passionate about building a better future and eager to shape a living, learning campus from




 the ground up. Join this team if you are interested in a purpose\-driven career.










**Job Description** 




 IIHS is looking for an experienced Construction Project Management professional to lead the




 campus construction works, which include coordination of the construction process during




 planning, design, and procurement as well as other pre\-construction activities.










 The role is not only that of a project manager but also includes the responsibilities of a




 reviewer of technical designs and BoQs. The person will work closely with external and




 internal structural engineers, architects, urban designers, MEP, ICT and IoT engineers, and




 project management teams to ensure that the construction is executed with precision within




 cost, schedule, quality, and sustainability parameters.










 The candidate will establish construction management processes, drive timely site decisions,




 ensure resource management and planning, and strive to achieve just\-in\-time availability of




 resources, and facilitate collaboration across multiple disciplines and practices.










**Activities and Tasks** 




 Responsibilities would include, but not be limited to, the following:



* Leading the planning, coordination, and execution of construction activities for the IIHS Kengeri campus as a sustainable, integrated residential, and institutional campus;
* Preparing and monitoring project schedules, milestones, phasing plans, work plans, and site deliverables to ensure timely project delivery;
* Supporting digital transformation initiatives like BIM and Digital Twin, SCADA, and IoT to use these digital tools effectively for better project management and control;
* Ensuring that the construction is delivered within approved timelines, budgets, quality standards, and statutory requirements in compliance with statutory requirements to meet sustainability objectives;
* Overseeing day\-to\-day site operations, contractors, consultants, vendors, and labour teams, with accountability for safety, quality, productivity, and sequencing;
* Coordinating civil, structural, MEP, ICT and IoT, landscape, roads, utilities, external development, renewable energy, water, wastewater, and campus service interfaces;
* Conducting regular site inspections and progress reviews to identify risks, delays, design interfaces, quality issues, and required corrective actions;
* Ensuring compliance with approved drawings, specifications, BOQs, design intent, building codes, and statutory requirements, including the review of technical submissions, shop drawings, method statements, material approvals, and test reports;
* Driving sustainable and climate\-responsive construction, including energy efficiency, passive design, thermal comfort, water conservation, low\-carbon materials, waste minimisation responsible sourcing;
* Supporting campus sustainability goals covering renewable energy, circular water systems, wastewater treatment, rainwater management, recycling, zero\-discharge principles, biodiversity, agroforestry, and ecological enhancement;
* Ensuring minimised impact of construction activities on the campus’ natural systems, including soil, vegetation, water resources and biodiversity, while maintaining a safe and healthy work environment;
* Monitoring project costs, quantities, variations, bills, claims, and contractor performance; supporting tendering, vendor evaluation, rate analysis, technical comparisons, and contract administration;
* Facilitating the digital and systematic documentation and publication of planning, design, construction, and system integration processes;
* Coordinating with architects, engineers, sustainability consultants, landscape teams, facilities, administration, finance, procurement, academic/research teams, and IIHS leadership to resolve project interfaces and decisions;
* Maintaining effective project controls and reporting through progress dashboards, risk registers, issue trackers, action logs, meeting records, inspection reports, compliance documentation, and sustainability records;
* Leading the testing, commissioning, snagging, rectification, as\-built documentation, statutory approvals, warranties, and final handover, while documenting lessons learned and enabling the campus to function as a living laboratory for sustainable development;
* Providing support to other IIHS activities including academics, research, training, practice, operations and others;
* Participating in all activities of Institution\-Building at IIHS; carrying out tasks as assigned by IIHS; and traveling on IIHS work within or outside the country as and when needed.









**Structure and Reporting** 




 The Senior Lead will report to the Head – Campus Development at the IIHS Kengeri Campus




 and will be required to collaborate effectively with a diverse group of internal teams and




 external individuals/ organisations, and students.










**Person Specification** 




 The ideal candidate should have:



* A Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering, and a Master’s degree in Construction/ Structural/ Civil Engineering is preferred;
* Around 20 years of experience in institutional, commercial, educational, mixed\-use, or large infrastructure projects;
* Experience working in institutional development and educational campus; this will be an advantage;
* Demonstrated experience in executing a large\-scale project of greater than 2 million square metres from inception to handover;
* Working knowledge of BIM\-enabled project delivery, including the use of BIM 4D and 5D tools, and multidisciplinary coordination;
* Exposure to sustainable development initiatives and vernacular construction techniques;
* Effective verbal and written communication skills;
* Flexibility and the ability to work well in a fast\-paced environment;
* Competency in multi\-tasking and managing multiple small project executions;
* Excellent organisational and team working skills; the ability and willingness to work in close collaboration with other teams to meet common institutional goals;
* Software skills:



 o AutoCAD:




 o MS Project/Primavera;




 o MS Office with a good hand at MS Excel;




 o ACC/ BIM 360 and other BIM tools (desirable);




 o AI application and prompt engineering.










 This offer is on an exclusive basis, which implies that other professional assignments (whether




 compensated or not) that bear a potential conflict of interest with IIHS cannot be undertaken.




 The search will remain open until the position is filled.










**Location** 




 This position is based in Kengeri, Bangalore and may entail travel to other locations in India.










**Review and Assessment** 




 The role and performance of the incumbent shall be subject to normal review and




 assessment systems at IIHS.










**Diversity Policy** 




 IIHS is an equal opportunity employer that encourages women, people with disabilities and




 those from economically and socially excluded communities with the requisite skills and




 qualifications to apply for positions.










**Contact** 




 Please write to us at careers@iihs.co.in if you need any clarifications while filling the online




 application form.
